{
	title: '/todo files a project TODO',
	spec: '/todo <item> records a TODO for the project of the session cwd. If TODO.md exists there it is the source of truth: the item is appended as "- <item>" (adding a missing final newline first), TODO.md alone is added if needed, and only that file is committed with the message "TODO: <item>" and the usual Implemented by (session model) and Session trailers, never other staged files (git commit -- TODO.md). Git failures are reported with a clear statement that the item remains saved; recording it does not depend on a successful commit. Without a TODO.md, the session is prompted "Add a TODO item to this project: <item>" so the model files it where the project keeps them; if the session is working it is not interrupted: a slot-free ordinary fork (task px) gets that prompt instead. Bare /todo shows the open items of TODO.md: plain Markdown bullets and unchecked checkboxes, excluding checked [x]/[X] bullets; when there is no TODO.md it reports that without starting model work.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Implemented in host/commands/todo.ts. Git uses argv, no shell; add and commit both carry only the TODO.md pathspec, so other staged changes remain staged even on a repository’s first commit. Bare listings include plain -/*/+ bullets as open items and omit checked boxes. Unlike old Hal, Git failures are visible and the saved item is explicitly retained.'
	],
	needs: ['x0', 'px']
